# Google Sign-In: OAuth 2.0 Web client ID (same value as backend GOOGLE_CLIENT_ID)
#
# The client ID alone is not enough. Google refuses to serve its button to an
# address that is not registered, with "The given origin is not allowed for the
# given client ID" in the console and a 403 on the button request.
#
# In Google Cloud Console -> APIs & Services -> Credentials -> the OAuth 2.0
# Web client, under "Authorized JavaScript origins", list every address the app
# is opened from:
#
#   http://localhost:5173                     local development
#   https://eduaust.austattendance.online     the deployed site
#
# Scheme, host and port must match exactly: http and https are different
# origins, and so are localhost and 127.0.0.1. The dev server is pinned to 5173
# (strictPort in vite.config.js) so this stays true. Changes can take a few
# minutes to take effect.
#
# Google only accepts plain http:// origins for localhost, so the deployed site
# has to be served over HTTPS before its origin can be registered at all.
VITE_GOOGLE_CLIENT_ID=495597854303-7cmdaf2rpkrb9l6gni8edc6u6np9sji1.apps.googleusercontent.com
